.TH CHROOTABLES-DESKTOP 1 "2026-10-27" "Chrootables" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
chrootables-desktop \- native workbench for local Debian image workspaces
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B chrootables-desktop
.RI [ --store " directory" ]
.RB [ --demo ]
.RI [ --screenshot " file" ]
.RB [ --version ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Chrootables creates Debian filesystem images, opens interactive terminals,
and manages clones, snapshots, disposable sessions, exports, and recovery.
Launch the desktop as your normal user. Store changes request administrator
access through a separate polkit helper. Terminal sessions authenticate with sudo.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --store " directory"
Use an absolute workspace store other than the host root directory.
The default is /var/lib/chrootable-manager.
.TP
.B --demo
Explore a read-only tour with sample workspaces.
.TP
.BI --screenshot " file"
Capture the window and exit; useful with --demo for verification.
.TP
.B --version
Print the application version and exit.
.TP
.B --help
Print command-line usage.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /var/lib/chrootable-manager
Default store containing images, snapshots, exports, archives, logs and history.
Store mutations require a root-owned directory that other users cannot write.
.SH NOTES
Workspaces run as host root and are intended for trusted development.
They are not security sandboxes for hostile code.
Disposable sessions discard image writes; writable shared host folders persist.
Removing the package leaves workspace data intact.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR chrootable-manager (1)
